 and genotype data as well as pedigree and person data.
 For completeness, Appendix A shows all the tables and their fields.
 Here, we will make a few general observations about the tables.
 The first issue was mentioned earlier: What should we do with pointers
 in C++.
 Where necessary, a field was added to a table, we call a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

link
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

