\begin_layout Paragraph
setRanges 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:applyFnToRanges"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Mega2R has an internal default list of the chromosome and base pair ranges
 for many gene transcripts.
 These transcripts come from the UCSC Genome Browser reference assembly
 GRCH37.
 The list was further modified to eliminate multiple records from the same
 gene with the exact same transcript start and transcript end.
 The list contains about 29,000 records.
 You may load your own range set instead of the default.
 You create a data frame that contains at least a name "observation", a
 chromosome "observation", a start position "observation" and an end position
 "observation".
 And you create an integer vector that contains the column numbers of the
 chromosome "observation", the start position "observation" and the end
 position "observation".
 These two become the arguments to the 
\emph on
setRanges
\emph default
 function, viz.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
setRanges(Ranges, Columns)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
applyFnToRanges
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The function:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
applyFnToRanges(DOcallback, envir = ENV) 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
goes through each transcript/range entry and finds the markers that fall
 within the bounds.
 It then builds a genotype matrix for the samples and each marker in the
 range.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The first argument of the 
\emph on
applyFnToRanges
\emph default
 function is a call back function.
 The function is called with four arguments: the genotype matrix, the markers
 in range, the selected transcript/range entry and the environment.
 The call back is invoked repeatedly for each transcript range that contains
 any markers.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If it is necessary to store information between successive invocations the
 environment ('envir') can be used.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\emph on
applyFnToRanges
\emph default
 can also be provided explicit ranges.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Flex Chunk
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

<<applyF2R,eval=FALSE>>=
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

applyFnToRanges(DOcallback, ENV$refRanges, ENV$refIndices, envir = ENV)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

applyFnToRanges(DOcallback, ENV$refRanges[ENV$refRanges$chromosome ==1,],
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

                ENV$refIndices, envir = ENV)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
setAnnotations
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Alternatively, you may search by genes.
 Here, the default transcript database is "TxDb.Hsapiens.UCSC.hg19.knownGene"
 from Bioconductor.
 Of course you can change it, by typing:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
setAnnotations("txdb", "genedb")
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
where "txdb" is a string that is the name of transcript database that was
 fetched from Bioconductor, and similarly "genedb" is the name of a Bioconductor
 database that maps a gene id from the transcript to an entrez gene id.
 The 
\emph on
setAnnotations
\emph default
 command must be issued whenever R is started and the Mega2R library has
 been loaded.
 By way of a reminder, Section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Bioconductor"

\end_inset

 explains how to choose and install "TxDb.Hsapiens.UCSC.hg19.knownGene" or a
 different Annotation database.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note: We could require that you add to your session
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
library(<name of the transcription database>)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
but we have chosen not to.
 Instead, you just indicate the database name and the logic of 
\emph on
applyFnToGenes
\emph default
 does a 'loadNamespace' of the name string and then a 'get' of the name
 string from the namespace.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
applyFnToGenes 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The function:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Flex Chunk
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

<<applyF2G,eval=FALSE>>=
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

applyFnToGenes(DOcallback, genes_arg = c('DISP1', 'KIF26B', 'AK5', 'ST7L'),
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

               envir = ENV)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
will find all the transcripts for each gene requested from the Bioconductor
 database.
 It will then call 
\emph on
applyFnToRanges
\emph default
: find all the markers in each transcript range, compute the genotype matrix
 and then invoke the call back function with the required four arguments.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\emph on
applyFnToGenes
\emph default
 function has several other optional arguments that can request complete
 chromosomes, (multiple) ranges of base pairs on chromosomes, or collections
 of markers in addition to the genes_arg argument.
 All these arguments define ranges that are passed to 
\emph on
applyFnToRanges
\emph default
 for evaluation.
 Note: If the 
\emph on
genes_arg
\emph default
 argument is set to the special "gene" string "*", then all transcripts
 in the Bioconductor database, will be processed.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Iterating through the Genotypes 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:Iterating-through-the"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Encoded Genotypes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The heart of the above two functions is the calculation of the genotype
 matrix of samples by markers containing the nucleotides (strings).
 The genotype information is most often stored in a compressed 2 bit representat
ion.
 An Rcpp function does the conversion of the compressed genotype data to
 nucleotides.
 The function
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
getgenotypes(markers, envir = ENV)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
returns the matrix for the specified markers.
 It can take one additional argument that supplies a string to separate
 the two alleles of each marker.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Raw Genotypes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The function
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
getgenotypesraw(markers, envir = ENV)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
is similar to the 
\emph on
getgenotypes
\emph default
 function except that the matrix it returns contains an integer encoding
 for each genotype.
 The integer's high 16 bits are the index for allele1 and the low 16 bits
 are the index for allele2.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note: There are actually two different Rcpp functions for each named function
 in Section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Iterating-through-the"

\end_inset

 One function processes compressed genotype data and the other function
 processes uncompressed genotype data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:pedgene"

\end_inset

 Using Mega2R to carry out automated gene-based association tests using
 'pedgene' 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Mega2R provides functions that permit one to run the 'pedgene' package to
 carry out gene-based association tests on 
\color black
family data looping over selected marker subsets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Loading a Mega2 database with 
\emph on
init_pedgene
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Rather than read the Mega2 SQLite database with the 
\emph on
read.Mega2DB
\emph default
 function, described previously, here we use a specialized 
\emph on
init_pedgene
\emph default
 function to read the Mega2 database.
 This latter function calls a utility function also used by 
\emph on
read.Mega2DB
\emph default
.
 Then it creates, edits, and rewrites the family data, storing it in a 'pedgene'
-compatible data frame, 
\series bold
fam
\series default
 .
 (
\series bold
fam
\series default
 merges data from the 
\series bold
pedigree_table
\series default
, 
\series bold
person_table
\series default
 and 
\series bold
phenotype_table
\series default
.) 
\emph on
init_pedgene
\emph default
 purges persons with unknown case/control status which is necessary for
 the pedgene calculation.
 (When 
\series bold
fam
\series default
 is updated, similar filtering is done to the persons in the 
\series bold
phenotype_table
\series default
 and the 
\series bold
genotype_table
\series default
.) Finally, 
\emph on
init_pedgene
\emph default
 calculates some values that will be used repeatedly and stores them in
 the environment that is returned.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Flex Chunk
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

<<init_pedgene,message=FALSE>>=
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

ENV = init_pedgene("seqsimr.db")
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Gene Ranges reminder 
