\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The genotype matrix for these markers, along with the markers, the range
 used, and the environment are passed to the call back function 
\emph on
DOpedgene
\emph default
.
 
\emph on
DOpedgene
\emph default
 converts the genotype nucleotides 1/1, 1/2 and 2/2 to the values 0, 1 and
 2 (or 2, 1, 0 if 1/1 is the genotype for the allele with the minor allele
 frequency).
 Then it runs 'pedgene'.
 The results are automatically stored in a data frame with "observations":
 prefix
\change_inserted -1820302391 1508527388
 data —
\change_deleted -1820302391 1508527395
 of
\change_unchanged
